                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/403: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-30T11:00:00-05:45">May 30, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>63. Department’s instruction No. 4, April 19th. President Moncada has just told
                    me that he approves draft note with amendments as stated in my air mail despatch
                    No. 45, May 23rd, and will direct the Foreign Office to submit the note.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
